  "text_sanskrit": "उदासीनवदासीनो गुणैर्यो न विचाल्यते । गुणा वर्तन्त इत्येवं योऽवतिष्ठति नेङ्गते ॥ १४-२३ ॥",
  "itrans": "udAsInavadAsIno guNairyo na vichAlyate . guNA vartanta ityevaM yo.avatiShThati ne~Ngate .. 14-23 ..",
  "translation": "He remains as if he were indifferent, who is not agitated by the Trigunas. He does not move, who firmly knows that the Gunas are only acting (under the Lord's direction). (23.) \nV. He is as if he were indifferent: but not really indifferent, since he is discharging the duties towards the Lord. He is not subject to the change which the influence of the Trigunas may produce. Avatisthati: firmly knows. Does not move: is not led to do actions which displease the Supreme Being. Thus the habit or course of conduct to be observed of the Gunatita is his constant attention only to the duties that delight the Lord.(23)",
